## Types

```mdl
type Notifications
  fields:
    feed: Ref<Feed>                       # messages, in arrival order; owned (SetParent)
    readIds: string[]                     # ids of read messages still in the feed
  typename: org.dxos.type.notifications
  version: 0.1.0
  note: |
    Not a user type, so it never appears in the navtree. One per default space, created by the
    materializer when it first stores a message; if two devices race, the lowest id wins.
```

```mdl
type StoredMessage
  base: org.dxos.type.message
  conventions:
    sender.identityDid: the verified envelope signer, never the payload's own claim
    attachments[].ref: the object the message points to; the first is opened on click
    properties.subject: subject line
    meta.keys: { source: "org.dxos.inbox", id: <envelope id> }   # dedupe across devices
```

## Capabilities

```mdl
component MessengerCapabilities.Sender
  desc: |
    `send(recipientDid, message): Effect<void, InboxSendError>`. Resolves the DID through the
    contact book (a DID cannot be turned back into an identity key), JSON-encodes the message and
    calls `client.halo.inbox.sendMessage`.
  errors: UnknownRecipientError | MessageSendError | InboxPayloadTooLargeError
```

```mdl
component MessengerCapabilities.NotificationsContainer
  desc: Atom of the default space's Notifications container, undefined until it exists.
```

```mdl
component InboxMaterializer
  desc: |
    Startup module (ClientEvents.SpacesAvailable). On every change to `halo.inbox.messages`,
    `halo.contacts` or `client.spaces`, runs one pass (passes never overlap):
      1. keep `org.dxos.inbox.message` messages from contacts; leave the rest pending;
      2. decode the payload (`Message.decodeJson`); ack undecodable payloads;
      3. skip messages whose envelope id is already stored (meta key), else append to the feed;
      4. flush, then ack every handled id.
    Toasts each newly written space invitation with a Join action.
```

## Components

```mdl
component NotificationTile
  desc: Mosaic tile — unread dot, subject, time; invitation surface or sender + text; menu.
  props:
    message: Message
    read: boolean
    renderInvitation?: (data, sender) => ReactNode
  emits:
    onAction(open | mark-read | mark-unread | delete)
```

```mdl
component NotificationsPanel
  desc: |
    Panel with a toggle-group filter (all / unread / invitations) and "Mark all as read", over a
    Mosaic.VirtualStack of NotificationTile, newest first. Click marks read and calls onOpen.
  props:
    notifications: Notifications
    renderInvitation?: InvitationRenderer
    onOpen?: (message) => void
```

```mdl
component MessengerCompanion
  desc: |
    Deck companion `messenger` (icon ph--envelope--regular). Renders invitations through
    `AppSurface.SpaceInvitation` (plugin-client) and opens the first attachment with
    `LayoutOperation.Open`. The companion's `badge` atom is the unread count.
```

## Operations

```mdl
op send
  key: org.dxos.operation.messenger.send
  desc: Sends a notification to a contact through MessengerCapabilities.Sender.
  input:
    recipientDid: string
    text: string
    subject?: string
    link?: Ref<Obj>
  output: void
  effects: [inbox:send]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Materialization
  req F-1.1:
    when: a contact's message arrives in the HALO inbox
    then: it is stored once in the default space's notifications feed and then acked
  req F-1.2:
    when: a message arrives from a non-contact
    then: it stays pending and is shown if the sender later becomes a contact
  req F-1.3:
    when: two devices of one identity receive the same envelope
    then: one copy is stored; both ack
  req F-1.4:
    when: a space invitation is stored
    then: the storing device shows a toast with Join; other devices do not
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Panel
  req F-2.1:
    when: there are unread notifications
    then: the envelope tab in R0 shows the unread count
  req F-2.2:
    when: the user clicks a notification
    then: it is marked read and its first linked object is opened
  req F-2.3:
    when: the user picks a filter
    then: only all / unread / invitation notifications are listed
  req F-2.4:
    when: the user chooses Mark as unread or Delete from a tile's menu
    then: the read state changes, or the message leaves the feed
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Sending
  req F-3.1:
    when: a plugin or agent sends to a contact's DID
    then: the message is relayed; non-contacts and oversized messages fail with typed errors
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Two users
  given: users A and B share a space (story Messenger/TwoUsers)
  when: A sends "Please review" to B
  then:
    - a tile appears in B's panel and B's badge reads 1
    - clicking the tile clears the badge
```

---

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: A contact's notification reaches the panel
  desc: Send from one identity, receive and read on another, through the storybook harness.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.2, T-1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - storybook is serving this worktree
  steps:
    - name: Open the two-user story
      do: Open the story plugins/plugin-messenger/Messenger/TwoUsers.
      expect: left column shows Alice's compose form; right column shows Bob's empty panel
    - name: Send
      do: Pick Bob as recipient, type "Please review", press Send.
      expect: a tile reading "Please review" appears in Bob's panel and the badge reads 1
    - name: Read
      do: Click the tile.
      expect: the badge clears
```
